---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import OwnGameSteps from '../components/OwnGameSteps.astro';
import { OWNER_URL, SOURCE_URL, SUGGEST_URL } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="about and legal"
  description="what a dreamport is, the bring-your-own-game rule, and the legal notes: dreamports is an unofficial fan project."
  current="about"
  currentIsPage
>
  <h1>about and legal</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    dreamports.net is a home for enhanced fan ports of classic games, made by a fan, for fans.
  </p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="dreamport">what a dreamport is</h2>
    <p>
      a dreamport is the port fans always dreamed of: the game you remember, with the extras you wished it
      had. it starts from the game as you know it, then adds the things fans have asked for over the years.
    </p>

    <h2 id="kinds">what you’ll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>dreamports.</strong> the ports made here, by <a href={OWNER_URL}>nahuel genchi</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>external ports.</strong> great ports made by other fans. dreamports links to their own pages and
        credits the people who made them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>other games.</strong> fan games that aren’t ports, like kirby’s dead land.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="own-game">bring your own game</h2>
    <p>
      dreamports never hosts game files: no <abbr class="caps" title="read-only memory">ROMs</abbr>, no game
      data and nothing taken from a game. it only lists projects that ask you to use your own legal copy, and
      before every play or download link it asks you to confirm that you are.
    </p>
    <OwnGameSteps />

    <h2 id="legal">not affiliated with any publisher</h2>
    <p>
      dreamports is an unofficial fan project. it is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by sega,
      nintendo or any other publisher. game names and trademarks belong to their owners, and appear here only
      to say which game a project works with.
    </p>
    <p>
      the site’s own design never uses publishers’ logos, box art or characters. pictures of games come only
      from the makers’ own recordings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="privacy">your privacy</h2>
    <p>
      there are no accounts, no ads and no cookies. the site keeps two small notes in your own browser: whether
      you chose dark mode, and, until you close the tab, which games you’ve confirmed you own. those notes never
      leave your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      to see which pages people read, the site counts visits with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">cloudflare web analytics</a>.
      it notes the page you opened, the site that sent you there, your browser, your country and how fast the
      page loaded. it stores nothing in your browser, doesn’t keep your ip address and doesn’t follow you to
      other sites.
    </p>

    <h2 id="credits">credits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>the site.</strong> made by <a href={OWNER_URL}>nahuel genchi</a>. its
        <a href={SOURCE_URL}>source code</a> is free to reuse under the mit license.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>type.</strong> headings are set in <a href="https://github.com/IdreesInc/Monocraft">monocraft</a>
        by idrees hassan, and the text in <a href="https://github.com/productiontype/Newsreader">newsreader</a>
        by production type, both under the sil open font license
        (<a href="/licenses/monocraft-OFL.txt">monocraft’s</a>, <a href="/licenses/newsreader-OFL.txt">newsreader’s</a>).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>the star.</strong> drawn by narik, from
        <a href="https://soulofkiran.itch.io/pixel-art-animated-star">pixel art animated star</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="contact">suggest a port, or report a problem</h2>
    <p>
      open an <a href={SUGGEST_URL}>issue on github</a>. it takes a free github account, and you don’t need to
      be a developer to fill it in. please never attach game files.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
